  "title": "Kirby Problem 3.26",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $M$ be a finite-volume hyperbolic 3-manifold, and let $M^1$ be a minimal-index finite cover of $M$ such that $\\pi_1(M^1)$ embeds in a right-angled Artin group. Can one obtain good control over the complexity of the smallest right-angled Artin group containing $\\pi_1(M^1)$ from the data of $M$?",
